WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.036
"How to Boost Your Endothelial Progenitor Cells (EPCs)
for Heart Health"

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.300
How can we remain
young at heart?

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.200
The capacity of our blood
vessels to repair themselves

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.340
is dependent on
endothelial progenitor cells

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.440
that emerge from stem cells
in our bone marrow

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.140
to patch up any holes
in our endothelium,

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.300
the innermost lining
of our blood vessels

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.160
that keeps our blood
flowing smoothly.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.300
Lower levels of circulating
endothelial progenitor cells

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.600
in the blood correlates
with arterial diseases

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.340
like erectile dysfunction.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.100
Higher numbers,
on the other hand,

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.500
are correlated with
a significantly reduced risk

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.660
of death
from cardiovascular causes.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.720
Before we explore
how to boost our levels,

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.480
let us first establish
cause-and-effect.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.440
A randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.880
was performed in men and women

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.860
with peripheral
vascular disease,

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.400
a circulation disorder
characterized by the narrowing

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.980
of blood vessels outside
of the heart or brain.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.920
The arteries supplying
blood to their legs

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.200
were so ravaged by disease

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.820
that they could only
walk about a minute

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:11.640
before the muscles in their legs
cried out in pain

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:12.960
from lack of oxygen.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.300
For each study participant,

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.580
one leg was randomly selected

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.160
to be injected with cells
from their own bone marrow

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.100
and the other was injected
with their own peripheral blood

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:23.820
as a control.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.500
Not only was pain-free walking
time significantly extended

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.180
in the marrow-injected leg,

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.560
they were less likely
to subsequently lose it.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.600
Severe limb ischemia,
lack of oxygen,

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.400
from peripheral
vascular disease

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.760
carries a 10 to 40 percent
amputation rate

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:42.960
within six months.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.520
In the control group,

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:48.480
14 percent were forced
to undergo a major amputation

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.900
compared to zero
in the bone marrow group.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.780
Given these remarkable benefits,

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.260
the link between higher numbers
of endothelial progenitor cells

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.780
and lower risk of dying
from cardiovascular disease

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.340
may indeed be causal.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.000
Short of sticking a large bore
needle into your hip,

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.400
how else can we
cultivate and release

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.460
more endothelial progenitor
cells into our system?

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.840
Smoking cessation is one of the
most important and effective

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.060
lifestyle changes to increase
the number and function

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:21.000
of active endothelial
progenitor cells.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.280
Cutting down isn't enough.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.440
There are 20 cigarettes
in a pack.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.300
If you only smoke
about one a day,

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.600
wouldn't you think you'd only
have one-twentieth the risk

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:31.800
of cardiovascular disease,

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.000
compared to smoking
the whole pack?

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.420
Based on a meta-analysis
of more than a hundred studies,

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.820
smoking only about
one cigarette a day

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:42.960
caused around 10 times the risk
of cardiovascular disease

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.760
you'd expect by that logic,

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.040
compared to smoking
a pack a day.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.880
There is no
safe level of smoking

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.220
when it comes to heart attack
and stroke risk.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:56.760
Even exposure to second-hand
smoke can deteriorate

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.340
our circulating endothelial
progenitor cell count,

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:03.060
so even just being
around smokers is risky.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.960
Randomized controlled trials
show exercise training

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.380
can actually boost endothelial
progenitor cell circulation.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.860
In a study of middle-aged
and older sedentary men,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.800
for example, three months
of moderate aerobic exercise--

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.960
mostly walking,
with some participants

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.480
starting to jog a bit
as their fitness improved--

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:25.140
led to a doubling of
endothelial progenitor cells

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.160
in their bloodstream.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.460
Regular aerobic exercise
could be considered

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:31.080
a "first line" strategy

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:34.200
for helping to prevent and treat
arterial aging.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.480
What about diet?

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:40.440
A randomized controlled trial
showed that reducing

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.080
saturated fat,
mostly in the form of butter,

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.940
significantly elevated

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.860
endothelial progenitor
cell numbers,

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:49.560
consistent with a study
on baboons showing that

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.600
even a few weeks
of a high-cholesterol,

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.820
high-fat diet
could cause dramatic

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:56.220
premature epithelial
cell senescence.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:00.000
Individual foods that
have been shown to increase

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.460
circulating endothelial
progenitor cells

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:06.900
include berries,
onions, and green tea,

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:09.960
and a diet centered completely
around whole plant foods

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.420
not only showed a boost
in endothelial progenitors,

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:14.760
but an improvement
in endothelial function,

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.640
along with a drop
in LDL cholesterol.

